WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:09.000
Successful economies and cultures are
built on trust. But a number of

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.900
high-profile data breaches and privacy
intrusions have caused anxiety for

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:17.400
consumers, and gotten the attention of
Washington. New legislation may be needed

00:00:17.400 --> 00:00:20.609
to bolster confidence in the digital
marketplace, but we've got to be

00:00:20.609 --> 00:00:23.699
thoughtful about it so we don't strangle
the golden goose that we call the

00:00:23.699 --> 00:00:27.000
Internet.
Three points: Explosive growth of digital

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.750
services shows that the benefits of data
flows far outweigh the costs.

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:34.290
Slow productivity growth in many
industries stems from a lack of

00:00:34.290 --> 00:00:38.399
information intensity —  too little data.
Policies should thus encourage the use

00:00:38.399 --> 00:00:42.870
of more data while putting consumers in
control of sensitive information. A new

00:00:42.870 --> 00:00:47.370
national privacy law would consolidate
existing industry specific laws, prevent

00:00:47.370 --> 00:00:51.420
a patchwork of conflicting state laws,
and clarify the FTC's enforcement

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.340
strategy for the digital age. But
regulations cannot solve every problem.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:59.969
Evolving social norms, more robust
institutions, and new privacy-promoting

00:00:59.969 --> 00:01:03.510
technologies will actually do most of
the heavy lifting of protecting our

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.320
privacy, and promoting data flows.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.520
Are you optimistic or pessimistic about the tech

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:14.120
economy? Let us know in our poll. Also, let
us know what other topics you'd like our

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:19.439
scholars to cover in 60 seconds, and be
sure to like and subscribe for more

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:23.240
research and videos from AEI.

